1
00:00:01,458 --> 00:00:03,375
SponsorScout. A final project film by Akshit

2
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:05,208
Verma, in four parts.

3
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:07,625
International students looking for data jobs

4
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,167
have a short clock,

5
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:12,158
and only some employers sponsor visas.

6
00:00:12,417 --> 00:00:14,283
So we apply to sponsors.

7
00:00:14,417 --> 00:00:16,667
But many of them have no entry-level

8
00:00:16,667 --> 00:00:18,250
data job open today,

9
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:20,833
and those applications go nowhere.

10
00:00:21,667 --> 00:00:22,667
SponsorScout tells the student,

11
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:23,750
for each sponsor,

12
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:24,917
whether to apply,

13
00:00:24,917 --> 00:00:26,875
network, check by hand,

14
00:00:26,875 --> 00:00:29,625
or skip, with the public record behind

15
00:00:29,625 --> 00:00:32,833
every answer. A strong sponsor with nothing

16
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:34,658
open isn't dropped.

17
00:00:34,708 --> 00:00:36,458
It goes on a networking list.

18
00:00:36,458 --> 00:00:37,375
It never applies,

19
00:00:37,375 --> 00:00:40,283
emails, or contacts anyone.

20
00:00:40,458 --> 00:00:41,950
The person decides.

21
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:44,458
I'm building it because I'm job hunting

22
00:00:44,458 --> 00:00:47,167
too, and I wanted a smarter strategy

23
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:49,708
than a hundred-plus applications a day.

24
00:00:49,708 --> 00:00:51,242
What already exists?

25
00:00:51,417 --> 00:00:53,625
My Visa Jobs lists sponsors and their

26
00:00:53,625 --> 00:00:55,292
past job counts;

27
00:00:55,292 --> 00:00:57,000
I looked at it in October.

28
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,708
H one B Grader grades employers on

29
00:00:59,708 --> 00:01:02,117
past approvals and denials.

30
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:04,583
Interstride, which universities provide,

31
00:01:04,583 --> 00:01:07,667
shows sponsorship history and filters jobs

32
00:01:07,667 --> 00:01:08,667
by visa.

33
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:11,167
The Reallocation Engine's own scorer,

34
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:13,000
which I had Claude Code run in

35
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,708
October, gives a sponsor with no open

36
00:01:15,708 --> 00:01:16,708
job a zero,

37
00:01:16,708 --> 00:01:18,075
and skips it.

38
00:01:18,125 --> 00:01:20,792
These tools show who sponsored before,

39
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:22,617
or what's open now.

40
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,708
None that I found turns a proven

41
00:01:24,708 --> 00:01:27,083
sponsor with nothing open into a networking

42
00:01:27,083 --> 00:01:29,167
target. That's the gap.

43
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:30,658
The data is public.

44
00:01:30,708 --> 00:01:32,875
Sponsorship records from the Eighty Days

45
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:34,283
to Stay file.

46
00:01:34,417 --> 00:01:37,458
Recent funding from S E C Form

47
00:01:37,458 --> 00:01:39,875
D filings. Open jobs from the public

48
00:01:39,875 --> 00:01:43,450
Greenhouse, Lever, and Ashby job boards.

49
00:01:43,583 --> 00:01:45,417
The job seeker is fictional.

50
00:01:45,417 --> 00:01:47,700
Each sponsor gets three checks:

51
00:01:47,708 --> 00:01:49,667
has it sponsored data roles,

52
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:51,667
has it raised money recently,

53
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:54,083
and is an entry-level data job open

54
00:01:54,083 --> 00:01:56,625
today? The answers set the verdict.

55
00:01:56,625 --> 00:02:00,042
The prototype ran on October third,

56
00:02:00,042 --> 00:02:02,292
on one hundred twenty-three sponsors.

57
00:02:02,292 --> 00:02:03,875
But only sixteen of them had a

58
00:02:03,875 --> 00:02:05,250
known job board,

59
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:07,825
so most answers were check by hand.

60
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,783
So, with Claude Code,

61
00:02:09,792 --> 00:02:11,658
I built a board resolver.

62
00:02:11,833 --> 00:02:14,083
It tries names built from each company's

63
00:02:14,083 --> 00:02:16,042
name, one request at a time,

64
00:02:16,042 --> 00:02:19,000
saves every raw response with a fingerprint,

65
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,667
and stops when it's done,

66
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:21,667
out of budget,

67
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:23,125
or hitting errors.

68
00:02:23,125 --> 00:02:24,700
It only proposes.

69
00:02:24,875 --> 00:02:27,458
I approve or refuse each board,

70
00:02:27,458 --> 00:02:29,125
and my decision is tied to the

71
00:02:29,125 --> 00:02:31,575
fingerprint of the response I saw.

72
00:02:31,708 --> 00:02:33,583
It can only read from those three

73
00:02:33,583 --> 00:02:35,458
sites, and it has no way to

74
00:02:35,458 --> 00:02:36,458
send anything.

75
00:02:36,458 --> 00:02:38,042
I have what I need:

76
00:02:38,042 --> 00:02:40,625
Claude Code, free public job boards,

77
00:02:40,625 --> 00:02:42,908
no keys, and no paid compute.

78
00:02:43,042 --> 00:02:45,500
Next, I'll re-run the verdicts on the

79
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,458
new boards, then evaluate them.

80
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:49,242
How will I know it worked?

81
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:52,250
First, coverage. On November twenty-third,

82
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:54,542
the resolver made six hundred twenty-nine

83
00:02:54,542 --> 00:02:57,500
requests, all to the three allowed sites,

84
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:00,042
and found candidate boards for thirty-nine

85
00:03:00,042 --> 00:03:02,992
companies. After my review,

86
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,917
coverage went from sixteen to fifty,

87
00:03:04,917 --> 00:03:05,950
of one hundred twenty-three.

88
00:03:06,875 --> 00:03:08,167
It also got things wrong,

89
00:03:08,167 --> 00:03:09,783
in ways I could check.

90
00:03:10,083 --> 00:03:12,083
Five boards belonged to other companies,

91
00:03:12,083 --> 00:03:14,033
like a childcare center.

92
00:03:14,292 --> 00:03:15,208
Claude flagged them,

93
00:03:15,208 --> 00:03:17,492
and I refused all five.

94
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:19,917
The name check called Weight Watchers a

95
00:03:19,917 --> 00:03:22,658
mismatch, though it's the right company.

96
00:03:22,875 --> 00:03:24,833
Five approved boards are empty,

97
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:27,792
and sixty-seven companies showed no board

98
00:03:27,792 --> 00:03:29,292
under the names it tried.

99
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:31,783
One bug got past every test.

100
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:33,083
On a Windows console,

101
00:03:33,083 --> 00:03:34,833
the command saved my approval,

102
00:03:34,833 --> 00:03:37,917
then crashed. A test now reproduces it,

103
00:03:37,917 --> 00:03:40,375
and all twenty-eight tests pass.

104
00:03:40,375 --> 00:03:41,875
Next, the verdicts.

105
00:03:41,875 --> 00:03:43,166
Before tuning anything,

106
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:44,958
I'll set aside a hand-checked set of

107
00:03:44,958 --> 00:03:47,750
sponsors. If fewer than nine in ten

108
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:50,041
apply verdicts are right on that set,

109
00:03:50,041 --> 00:03:51,158
it didn't work.

110
00:03:51,333 --> 00:03:52,916
And after fourteen days,

111
00:03:52,916 --> 00:03:54,958
I'll re-check the networking targets for

112
00:03:54,958 --> 00:03:57,750
new postings. This sample can show what

113
00:03:57,750 --> 00:03:58,825
it gets wrong.

114
00:03:58,958 --> 00:04:01,416
It can't show that anyone gets hired.

115
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:04,541
SponsorScout. A film by Akshit Verma.

